      "report_date": "2026-11-11",
      "title": "Off the Rails: Inside an Exposed Silent Lynx Server",
      "summary": "Silent Lynx, a Central Asia-focused espionage cluster, was exposed through an open directory on a server that CloudSEK analysed, covering activity from April to October 2026. The directory held implant builds for Laplas and Chvost families, delivery kits built on LNK shortcuts and PowerShell reverse shells, and victim data. The operator had domain-level access to Tajikistan's national railway and used one compromised railway employee account to pull thousands of government documents, many tied to the Ministry of Defence, from Tajikistan's document management platform. Intrusions also reached an Uzbek GeoServer host, and lures impersonating Turkmen railway and regional administration bodies pointed to a planned campaign against Turkmenistan. The operator ran much of the work through a self-hosted DeepSeek-based AI agent, and test sessions from a residential Kazakh ISP connection support a medium-confidence Kazakhstan nexus.",
      "completeness": "High",
      "threats": [
