      "report_date": "2026-11-11",
      "title": "Trigram Campaign",
      "summary": "Stormshield attributes the Trigram campaign with high confidence to North Korea, as a continuation of the UNK_DeadDrop cluster and the Kimsuky group. The actors impersonate about 50 brands in the blockchain, AI, and logistics sectors through fake recruitment, conference invitation, and package-tracking sites. Victims are tricked via a ClickFix-style fake verification step into pasting a command that is silently swapped in the clipboard to download and run a malicious script. The payload is a JavaScript loader that deploys an infostealer targeting browser credentials and cryptocurrency wallets. A campaign management platform automates GitHub-based target collection, bulk email delivery across four providers, and real-time victim tracking.",
      "completeness": "High",
