      "report_date": "2026-11-11",
      "title": "Analysis of a Wpcdoor Attack Distributed Through Domestic DVR Management Software",
      "summary": "The Wpcdoor backdoor was distributed through the CMS (Central Management Software) of a domestic Korean DVR and CCTV vendor, as reported by Huntress and confirmed by AhnLab's ASD logs showing infections in Korea. The attack chain runs through rs.win32.exe, where a malicious IPHLPAPI.DLL is side-loaded and acts as a downloader for WpcMon.exe and samcli.dll, which in turn fetches the final Wpcdoor backdoor and runs it in memory. Wpcdoor can steal system information, capture screenshots and clipboard data, grab files, dump browser data and cryptocurrency wallet-related memory, and enable remote control. AhnLab tracks the actor as Larva-26013, which has also deployed Wpcdoor in other campaigns. Defenders should apply vendor patches, review the configuration of the affected software, and immediately change IDs and passwords used in the software and connected systems.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
