      "report_date": "2026-11-11",
      "title": "The XG Files: Falcon C2 Flying Under The (Browser) Radar",
      "summary": "Unit 42 describes Falcon (aka XG), a NodeJS command and control framework that compromises browsers by running malicious JavaScript on webmail and government web applications. The framework can sideload a malicious Chrome extension disguised as a PDF viewer to steal passwords, emails, session cookies and communications. Falcon also delivers the Rust-based Antino implant, which uses Microsoft OneDrive as a C2 channel. Campaigns between March and May 2026 compromised government entities in one Middle Eastern country and several Southeast Asian countries, targeting foreign affairs, defense, interior and law enforcement ministries. Defenders should monitor for developer-mode extensions with broad permissions, unexpected Hm_lvt_ cookies, and unfamiliar external script tags on internal portals.",
      "completeness": "High",
