      "report_date": "2026-11-11",
      "title": "Field Intelligence #5: Scareware at scale. Investment scams built on AI platforms.",
      "summary": "ZoidWays is a mobile scareware forced-redirect campaign tracked since March, reaching about 1.5 million blocked impressions in one day across at least six ad buying platforms. Victims see a fake phone-settings clone with a bogus \"Platform Security for wiretapping\" alert that leads to antivirus checkouts, paid support lines, or subscription traps. The report also covers a fake Microsoft Teams APK that functions as a remote access trojan, harvesting cryptocurrency seed phrases via clipboard, filesystem, and OCR scanning. PseudoCamo runs investment scams on AI app-builder platforms, with cloaked age-gate landing pages that redirect to second-hop money pages across multiple countries. D-Shortiez has shifted its tech-support scams to BunnyCDN and Azure hosts and added a fake CAPTCHA step that resembles ClickFix but is a forced redirect. A Claude-branded \"trading bot\" scam tricks UK victims into moving their own funds through a MetaMask contract that forwards the balance to the scammer.",
