      "report_date": "2026-11-11",
      "title": "Inside The Server: 14 Months of Offensive Cyber Operations Targeting Europe",
      "summary": "Group-IB discovered an open directory on a Latvian server exposing the working environment of a threat actor it tracks as DarkLunnen, containing over 14 months of offensive operations against Europe. The operator, apparently still active at discovery, used a modified watchTowr proof-of-concept for FortiGate CVE-2024-55591 to create a backdoor \"service\" super-admin account across devices in Turkey, Ukraine, Azerbaijan, and Algeria. Other activity included VNC brute-forcing that reached apparent HMI systems, scanning of Hikvision cameras, and attempted source code collection from Ukrainian defense and aviation organizations. Group-IB has not attributed the operator to a known actor, and only 35 of 457 files were recovered. Defenders should patch edge devices, rotate secrets on any exposed device, and restrict VNC, camera, and remote management interfaces.",
