      "report_date": "2026-11-11",
      "title": "Online Casino Serves Malicious Python SDK",
      "summary": "The malicious PyPI package aurum-pay (version 1.2.0) presents itself as a working payment SDK for an online casino, but its first real API request silently fetches a command from the casino's domain and runs it. On Linux, that command downloads and launches \"RCMD Remote Agent,\" a remote access trojan that installs persistence as a fake Chromium systemd service. The trojan connects to a hard-coded controller and gives the operator shell access, file transfer, reconnaissance, and screenshots. Because the SDK's default host also receives API keys and customer payment data, applications using the package may have exposed sensitive information as well. Defenders should assume compromise of any host that ran aurum-pay and check for the listed persistence files and network connections.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
